+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate`. It used `unit_price * rate`, so quantity was ignored (PRICING.md rule 3).
+  - `Invoice.add` raises `ValueError` for any rate name not in `RATES` (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: `test_reduced_rate_small_item` was wrong, so I changed it. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52. By rule 4, 0.50 * 0.05 = 0.025, which rounds half up to 0.03, so gross is 0.53. I updated the test to 0.03 and 0.53.
+
+## Verified
+- Before the changes, `python -m unittest` ran 6 tests and 4 failed.
+- After the changes, `python -m unittest` ran 6 tests, all OK.
+- I checked the other test expectations (pen, mixed rates) by hand against PRICING.md and they agree.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not change `docs/PRICING.md` or any file outside `billing/`, `tests/` and `SUMMARY.md`.
+- I did not add tests for rounding edge cases beyond the existing ones.
+- The sticker test's old 0.02 looks like banker's rounding or a float artifact, which would contradict the signed-off half-up rule. Worth confirming nobody relied on that figure.
